                    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions: Building Credit From Zero (US)</h2>
                    <h3>Can I build credit with no SSN?</h3>
                    <p>Yes for revolving: Chime Credit Builder requires SSN but some secured cards accept ITIN. Rent reporters like Boom accept ITIN. For official SSN-free building, you need ITIN + bank that reports. Self requires SSN/ITIN.</p>
                    <h3>What credit score do you start with? Is 0 real?</h3>
                    <p>No US bureau gives you 0. You start with no file. After first account reports for 1 month, VantageScore can be ~630-670. FICO requires 6 months (CFPB). So “0 to 700” is marketing shorthand for “invisible to good.”</p>
                    <h3>Does Self charge interest?</h3>
                    <p>Self accounts include admin fee and interest at ~15.92% APR on small build plans, but you get money back minus fees at end. Check latest at Self.inc. The fee is the cost of installment reporting — still cheaper than secured card interest if you carry balance.</p>
                    <h3>How fast can I get to 700?</h3>
                    <p>With 100% on-time payments, <10% utilization, and 2-account mix, median US user hits 670-700 by month 12 per Experian analysis of credit-builder users. No lates, no inquiries=faster.</p>
                    <h3>Which accounts report to all 3 bureaus?</h3>
                    <p>Both Chime Credit Builder and Self Credit Builder report to Experian, Equifax, TransUnion. Always confirm “reports to all 3” before opening — required by our ScoreUp methodology.</p>
                    <h3>Do I need to carry a balance to build?</h3>
                    <p>No. FICO does not reward interest. Pay full statement balance. Carrying balance only adds APR fees — cited by Equifax and CFPB as myth.</p>

